
== A  the even native class: G16 and Gbig
PASS A1  [enumerate] each of the distinct native gates (actC D o cnot o actC D' o actT R0) has exactly one orientation pair over all 4096 signed-diagonal dressings
PASS A2  [enumerate] 8 native gates are (even, even), cnot among them; they generate a group G16 of order 16 containing cnot
INFO |even locals| = 32, |Gbig| = |<cnot, even locals>| = 64; G16 <= Gbig: True
PASS A3  [enumerate] 32 distinct orientation-even signed-diagonal locals; G16 is a subgroup of Gbig = <cnot, even locals>

== B  Gbig <= Aut(Q3): every element is L or cnot o L with L an even local; even locals are Pauli conjugations or the full transpose composed with them
PASS B1  [enumerate] every element of Gbig equals L or cnot o L with L one of the 32 even locals
PASS B2  [identity] actC/actT of diag(1,-1,-1), diag(-1,1,-1), diag(-1,-1,1) = conjugation by X, Y, Z on that qubit, symbolic
PASS B3  [identity] actC reflY o actT reflY = full transpose: pauliW(T w) = pauliW(w)^T, symbolic; and every even local with det D = det E = -1 equals (actC reflY o actT reflY) o (a det +1 local)
PASS Bc  [countercontrol] countercontrol: the odd local actC reflY is rejected: not in Gbig, not of the form L or cnot o L, and it maps the Bell table phiW to a non-PSD table (<s|.|s> = -1 on the singlet s = |01> - |10>)

== C  the four defects: stabilizer basis, tables, spectra, Gram matrix, permutation by Gbig
PASS C1  [identity] psi_s orthonormal, X(x)Z psi_s = s1 psi_s, Y(x)Y psi_s = s2 psi_s
PASS C2  [identity] T_s = E00 + s1 E13 + s2 E22 + s1 s2 E31 (pure tables of psi_s)
PASS C3  [identity] pauliW(e_s) = (1/8)(I - 2 psi_s psi_s^T) for all four s (SD1 hypothesis, beta = 1/8, g = psi_s)
PASS C4  [identity] ipW(e_s, e_t) = 1/4 if s = t, else 0 (pairwise orthogonal defects; subdual set)
PASS C5  [enumerate] every element of Gbig (hence of G16) permutes {T_s}, hence permutes the defect set X
PASS Cc  [countercontrol] countercontrol: the permutation test rejects the odd local actC reflY (some T_s is mapped outside {T_t})

== D  H1 for K4 over the continuous product family (symbolic)
PASS D1  [identity] ipW(e_s, prodState x y) = (1 - x^T M_s y)/4 with M_s y = (s1 y3, s2 y2, s1 s2 y1), symbolic
PASS D2  [identity] 2(1 - x^T M_s y) = |x - M_s y|^2 + (1 - |x|^2) + (1 - |y|^2), symbolic (|M_s y| = |y|): every e_s is in maxCone, so SEP <= Q3 n X^*; cnot X = X (C5) gives cnot SEP <= Q3 n X^* too
PASS Dc  [countercontrol] countercontrol: the H1 test rejects e'_s = (1/8)(I - 3 psi_s psi_s^T) (table E00/2 - 3 T_s/8): ipW(e'_s, prodState((s1,0,0), (0,0,1))) = -1/4 < 0

== F  the witness pair for K4 != Q3; G  E0 is not G16-invariant and not in K4
PASS F1  [witness] each e_s is not PSD (psi_s^T pauliW(e_s) psi_s = -1/8) and ipW(e_s, T_s) = -1/2 with T_s = P_v, v = 2 psi_s an integer vector, pauliW(T_s) = psi_s psi_s^T
PASS F2  [witness] each T_s is not a product table and cnot T_s is not a product table (ranks > 1)
PASS G1  [witness] some g in G16 has ipW(E0, g E0) = -1: no G16-invariant subdual cone contains E0 (K1 is a level-(i) model only)
PASS G2  [witness] ipW(E0, e_(1,-1)) = -1/4 < 0: E0 is not in the self-dual K4 (K1 and K4 are different cones)

kinds: identity 8, enumerate 5, witness 4, countercontrol 3
VERDICT X3-G16-K4-EXACT -- 20 checks
